# OPTIONAL build-time defaults. Leave both empty for a distributable build.
#
# Credentials are now configured IN THE APP: open /setup and paste your project URL and anon key.
# They are stored on the device, so the installed desktop app can be pointed at a project (or
# re-pointed later) without a rebuild, which NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables cannot do - they are inlined
# by the bundler at build time.
#
# Set these only for a fixed single-shop deployment that should be pre-configured out of the box.
# Stored settings in the app always win over these values.
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# The "anon" / "publishable" key. Safe in the browser: row level security protects the data.
# NEVER put the service_role or secret key here - the app refuses it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DESKTOP INSTALLER (read by `npm run desktop:config`, which every `npm run dist*` runs first)
#
# Fill these in to build an installer that is already connected, so the shopkeeper never sees the
# setup screen. Leave them empty for a generic installer that asks for them on first launch.
# Both or neither: setting only one is a build error.
#
# These are NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_* on purpose. Those are inlined by the bundler, which would bake this
# shop's project into the public website build. These become a file inside the installer instead,
# so the same source tree still deploys an unconfigured website.
#
# Works in `.env`, `.env.local`, or the shell; the shell wins. Precedence inside the app:
#   project saved on this machine  >  this shipped project  >  NEXT_PUBLIC_* above
# `Disconnect` on /setup sticks, so a preconfigured till will not silently reconnect itself.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POS_SUPABASE_URL=
POS_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC WEBSITE (vendor registration, migration 0029). Optional; website build only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Name shown on the landing and registration pages. Defaults to "Smart POS".
NEXT_PUBLIC_PLATFORM_NAME=
# Cloudflare Turnstile site key for the human check on /register. Public by design. Put the matching
# SECRET in Supabase -> Authentication -> Attack Protection (CAPTCHA), never here. Empty = no widget.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
